			"notes": "Floating Rock rebuilt from hanging columns; new Fluted Rock tool\n\nFloating Rock:\n- Top outline is a polygon: every rim column is one flat face, some stick out\n- Rock = concentric rings of flat-faced columns hanging from the top; outer columns\n  short, inner long -> stepped taper like hand-built rock assets\n- Silhouette: Taper, Straight Wall Height, Tip Thickness, Lobes\n- Columns: width/variation, depth step, wobble, offset, length variation,\n  long drip columns, cleanup (no 1-wide strips); scale with radius\n- Twist rotates layers, Lean shifts them\n\nFluted Rock (new): radius profile (top width, bulge, rounded top/base, sink) with\nbillow flutes stretched along Y (rounded ribs, sharp grooves) + fine flutes, twist,\nlumps; ribs fade on the rounded top, floating bits removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
