			"notes": "Floating Rock: per-side stretch, tip thickness, voxel cleanup, mound follows the top outline\n\n- Replace Width X/Z Ratio with Stretch East/West/South/North (+X/-X/+Z/-Z) on top of Radius/Height\n- Tip Thickness + Tip Rounding: the spike can end in a thick rounded cap instead of a point\n- Plate offsets are capped by the local radius, so the thin tip no longer breaks into loose blocks\n- Smoothing pass: 3x3 majority per layer, Min Step Height per column, despeckle of lone blocks\n- Top Mound is a smooth height field from the real top outline (distance to edge + low noise),\n  never placed over air; new Mound Spread / Mound Bumps / Bump Size\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
